\label{fig:lightcone_10x10}
\end{figure}

Figure~\ref{fig:lightcone_10x10} shows the spatial evolution at $\chimax=50$.
Three phases are clearly visible.
First, ballistic expansion ($t \lesssim 1.4$): the weight front grows as a
Manhattan-distance diamond consistent with a Lieb-Robinson velocity of
$v_{\rm LR} \approx 1$ lattice site per $\delta t$.
Second, boundary reflection ($t \approx 2.0$--$2.4$): the front reaches all
four edges simultaneously (C4 symmetry of the even-site center is approximate
here; the $10\times10$ center is at $(4,4)$, slightly off-center) and the
reflected wave interferes constructively at the ring of sites at Manhattan
distance $d_{\max}$ from the center.
Third, scrambling ($t \gtrsim 2.5$): the ring disperses and weight becomes
increasingly uniform.

